<title>MOLDOVA: Moldovan T-bills mixed at auction.</title>
<headline>Moldovan T-bills mixed at auction.</headline>
<dateline>CHISINAU 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised yield on Moldovan 28-day Treasury bills remained at 17.17 percent on Tuesday, unchanged from the previous auction on July 8, the National Bank said.</p>
<p>The yield on 91-day T-bills fell to 17.58 percent from 18.46 percent on July 8. The yield on 182-day T-bills rose to 21.05 percent from 18.87 percent and the yield on 364-day T-bills rose to 22.01 percent from 19.10 percent.</p>
<p>Full details of the 28-day T-bill auction:</p>
<p>				    July 15	    July 8</p>
<p> Issue volume		   2.00 million lei     2.00 million lei</p>
<p> Denominations		  1,000 lei	  1,000 lei</p>
<p> Nominal demand		 3.69 million	   4.04 million</p>
<p> Volume sold		    2.00 million	   2.00 million</p>
<p> Yield			    17.17 pct	  17.17 pct</p>
<p> Price			    98.7 pct	   98.7 pct</p>
<p> Range of bids		  98.7-99.5 pct    98.7-99.2 pct</p>
<p> Maturity			 Aug 14, 1997     Aug 7, 1997</p>
<p>Full details of the three-month T-bill auction:</p>
<p>				    July 15	    July 8</p>
<p> Issue volume		   11.00 million	  14.00 million</p>
<p> Denominations		  1,000 lei	  1,000 lei</p>
<p> Nominal demand		 25.66 million	  17.39 million</p>
<p> Volume sold		    11.00 million	  14.0 million</p>
<p> Yield			    17.58 pct	  18.46 pct</p>
<p> Price			    95.8 pct	   95.6 pct</p>
<p> Range of bids		  95.8-96.6 pct    95.6-96.3 pct</p>
<p> Maturity			 Oct 16, 1997     Oct 9, 1997</p>
